── detail · server ──
CHECKED
not checked yet

NOW
https://gitlab.com

The GitLab server radar talks to.

ACCEPTS
https://gitlab.com or your own server's address

config: [gitlab] url

§ :connection: GET A GITLAB TOKEN
  1 Open GitLab's new-token page:
  gitlab.com / new token   open · copy
  name radar · scope from access: read_api
  2 Pick an expiry date, then Create personal access token.
  3 Copy the glpat-… value into token, or keep it out of radar's config:
  $ export GITLAB_TOKEN=glpat-…
  then the token is env:GITLAB_TOKEN
§ :terminal: ALREADY USE GLAB?
  Type glab as the token. Not signed in?
  $ glab auth login
§ :site: YOUR OWN GITLAB
  Set server first; the link above then points at your server's page.
§ :warning: IF IT IS REFUSED
  Expired, or without read_api: make a new one with the link.
  radar shows GitLab's own reason.
§ :link: MORE
  GitLab docs: access tokens
  radar guide: connect GitLab
